// The checker's type relation and what it is built from: `assignable`, the joins, type
// substitution and generic binding, annotation resolution (`nameToTy`/`tsToTy`), and the
// diagnostic sink (`tErr*`) every check reports through. These are one strongly connected set,
// so they share a module. Nothing here walks a node by kind: where a relation needs the core
// checker (an operator's pending return, a `??` default) it calls `checkerForceFn`, which
// `checkProgramPass` installs.

